course: dictionary
lesson: 10814
title: Meat words from farm to table
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Veal is the meat from a young calf, which is a baby cow. You will see it on restaurant menus, so it is a food word, not a word for an animal you could pet.
explain: Context gives you clues. On a menu you might read «veal cutlet», «veal escalope» or «roast veal». Each phrase names a meal, and the meal is made of veal. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Meat from a calf fits.
explain: Some people choose not to eat veal because of how young calves are kept. Farming rules have changed to help them, so the way veal is made is an important question in lessons about food and farming.
fact: Veal is the meat from a young calf, a baby cow.
fact: Veal is an uncountable noun, so we say some veal, not a veal.
fact: Wiener schnitzel is one dish that can be made with veal.
fact: «Veal» comes from the French word veau, which means calf.
fact: Some people choose not to eat veal, because of how young calves are kept on farms.
exercise: What is veal? | A young calf, a baby cow | A kind of cheese | *Meat from a young calf | A young pig
exercise: «Beef comes from bœuf, pork from porc, mutton from mouton and veal (calf meat) from veau.» Which French word does veal come from? | bœuf | porc | *veau | mouton
exercise: Which of these dishes is made with veal? | Apple crumble | Cheese on toast | *Wiener schnitzel
test: The menu offers «veal escalope». What is veal? | Milk from a cow | *Meat from a young calf | A kind of bread | A green vegetable
test: Which sentence uses veal correctly? | We ate veals and dinner. | We ate a veal and milk for dinner. | *We ate some veal for dinner. | Veal dinner we ate the.
exam: Why might some people choose not to eat veal? | Because it is always cold | Because it grows on trees | *Because of how young calves are kept | Because it is too sweet
